WHAT THIS COVERS

The prose and images under `content/` — the posts, the project pages, and any
media stored beside them.

It does NOT cover the source code, configuration and templates elsewhere in
this repository, which are licensed under the MIT License — see `LICENSE` at
the repository root.


THE GRANT

You are free to:

  Share  — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format
  Adapt  — remix, transform, and build upon the material

for any purpose, even commercially, under the following terms:

  Attribution — You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the
  licence, and indicate if changes were made. You may do so in any reasonable
  manner, but not in any way that suggests the licensor endorses you or your
  use.

  No additional restrictions — You may not apply legal terms or technological
  measures that legally restrict others from doing anything the licence
  permits.


THE FULL LEGAL TEXT

The authoritative legal code is published by Creative Commons at:

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

and the human-readable summary of it at:

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Referencing the canonical text is the method Creative Commons itself
recommends for applying one of its licences, and it is used deliberately here
rather than pasting a copy: an inaccurately reproduced licence is worse than a
precise reference to the authoritative one, and the legal code is the kind of
document that must not drift.

This is a difference from the MIT licence at the repository root, where the
text IS the grant and is therefore reproduced in full.

Note for the avoidance of doubt: the URLs above are references in a plain text
file. They are not subresources, and nothing in the published site fetches
them — no page causes a visitor's browser to contact any host other than the
one serving the site.


FONTS ARE SEPARATE

Font files shipped with the site carry their own licence, which travels with
the files themselves (open font licences generally require this). Neither this
file nor the MIT licence at the root governs them.
